Keep infinity and NaN off awk's integer formatting, which writes numbers
with "%.0f": msvcrt formats infinity as "1.#INF" and rounds that to "1"
at zero precision, so "print log(0)" printed -1. An infinite value now
goes through OFMT or CONVFMT, as before FRP-6354, and printf's integer
conversions write infinity and NaN with %g. Also print a zero integer as
0, not -0, as before.

